# DelayDetectives

**SE3513 Introduction to Machine Learning** — Predicting Flight Arrival Delays

Predict how late a US domestic flight will arrive, using only information that is known before the flight.
Models are compared against a simple median baseline. The final model will be used in a website.

- **Data:** [2015 Flight Delays and Cancellations](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/usdot/flight-delays) (USDOT, CC0). Not stored in this repo.
- **Split:** by day, stratified by month — in every month, 70% of the days go to train, 15% to validation, 15% to test (all flights of a day stay together). This replaced a first month-based split (train Jan–Aug, validation Sep–Oct, test Nov–Dec), which gave very different parts; see [Phase 3](reports/phase3_report.md).
- **Tasks:**
  - Regression: arrival delay in minutes (metric: MAE)
  - Classification: will the flight be more than 15 minutes late? (metrics: accuracy, precision, recall, F1, ROC-AUC)

## Repository layout

| Folder | Content |
|---|---|
| `src/` | Code for each phase, run on Kaggle (`phase0_...py`, `phase1_...py`, ...) |
| `reports/` | One report per phase |
| `results/` | Small outputs: tables and plots |
| `model/` | Final models and tables for the website (Phase 8); used with `src/predict.py` |
| `docs/` | Original project plan |

